        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "hashcat fails to restrict command-line options when parsing restore files, allowing attackers to inject output-redirecting options like --outfile and --potfile-path. Attackers can craft restore files with malicious options to append attacker-controlled content to arbitrary files, enabling code execution when targeting shell startup files.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
